## Application shell (Stage 03)

Permanent structural framework. Future sections require **only their own
content** — no structural changes.

- **Header** — fixed, transparent by default, gains `.is-scrolled` (solid +
  shadow) past an 8px threshold; collapses to a mobile trigger ≤768px. Slots:
  `logo`, `primary-nav`, `cta`, `menu-trigger` (all empty placeholders).
- **Main** (`.site-main#main`) — flex column; the container for all sections.
- **Footer** — placeholder regions: brand, quick-links, services, contact,
  newsletter (optional), social, copyright, legal.

### Section pattern (for every future section)

```html
<section class="section" id="hero" data-section aria-labelledby="hero-title">
  <div class="container">
    <!-- section content -->
  </div>
</section>
```

Section modifiers: `--soft` / `--tinted` / `--inverse` (background),
`--center`, `--divider-top` / `--divider-bottom`, `--flush` / `--compact`,
`--full`, `--below-header`.

Containers: `.container` (default, 1280), `.container--narrow` (820),
`.container--wide` (1440), `.container--full` (edge-to-edge).

### Scroll architecture (prepared, not animated)

Smooth scroll + sticky-header anchor offset (`scroll-padding-top`),
`[data-reveal]` → `.is-inview` reveal contract, and a `[data-section][id]`
scroll-spy that sets `body[data-active-section]` for future active-nav states.
All respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.

> Dev aid: add `class="shell-debug"` to `<body>` to outline empty slots.

## The one rule

**Never hardcode values in components or sections.** Everything references a
token from `tokens.css`. Color, type, spacing, radius, shadow, border, motion,
z-index, opacity — all of it flows from the token layer so the whole site stays
consistent and is trivial to tune globally.

## How to include (when sections are built)

Link in this order — tokens first, so global styles can reference them:

```html
<link rel="stylesheet" href="styles/tokens.css">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="styles/global.css">
```

### Fonts — Cairo (Google Fonts)

Load in the `<head>` with `preconnect` (better performance than `@import`).
Cairo is used across the **entire** interface and includes full Arabic support.

```html
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<link rel="stylesheet"
  href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Cairo:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap">
```

Weights in use: **400** (regular), **500** (medium), **600** (semibold),
**700** (bold). The font stack in `--font-family-base` falls back to system
sans + `Noto Sans Arabic` if Cairo is unavailable.

## Token reference (quick map)

| Group | Prefix | Notes |
|------|--------|------|
| Color — semantic | `--color-*`, `--surface-*`, `--text-*` | Reference these, not raw `--brand-*` |
| Typography | `--font-*`, `--leading-*`, `--tracking-*` | Fluid sizes via `clamp()` |
| Spacing | `--space-*` | 8pt rhythm (4 → 160) |
| Layout | `--container-*`, `--section-padding-y` | 1280px cap · 80px pad · 140px section |
| Grid | `--grid-columns`, `--grid-gutter` | 12 → 8 → 4 across breakpoints |
| Radius | `--radius-*` | Semantic: button/input/card/image/modal |
| Elevation | `--shadow-*` | Subtle, cool-tinted (none → floating/hover) |
| Border | `--border-*` | Divider, input, card |
| Motion | `--duration-*`, `--ease-*`, `--transition-*` | Refined, minimal |
| Z-index | `--z-*` | Single ordered scale |
| Opacity | `--opacity-*` | |
| Breakpoints | `--bp-*` | Reference values (mirrored in media queries) |

## Layout primitives available now

- `.container` (+ `.container--narrow`) — centered, capped, fluid padding
- `.section` (+ `--soft` / `--tinted` / `--inverse`) — vertical rhythm
- `.grid` + `.col-1 … .col-12` — Swiss grid, responsive column counts
- Utilities: `.u-stack`, `.u-list-reset`, `.u-measure`, `.u-visually-hidden`,
  `.skip-link`

## Responsive approach

**Desktop-first.** Type and spacing scale fluidly via `clamp()`; structural
media queries (`max-width`) step the grid down at **1200 / 768 / 480**.
`prefers-reduced-motion` is fully respected.

## Accessibility

Sufficient contrast, visible keyboard focus (`:focus-visible`), readable type,
comfortable spacing, 44px minimum touch targets, RTL/Arabic-aware letter
spacing, and a skip-to-content link.
